              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "User-controlled data flows into EF.Property(). If attackers control the property name, this enables dynamic field access and ORM leak-style inference."
              },
              "help": {
                "markdown": "User-controlled data flows into EF.Property(). If attackers control the property name, this enables dynamic field access and ORM leak-style inference.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/203.html](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/203.html)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/A01_2021-Broken_Access_Control/](https://owasp.org/Top10/A01_2021-Broken_Access_Control/)\n - [https://www.elttam.com/blog/leaking-more-than-you-joined-for/](https://www.elttam.com/blog/leaking-more-than-you-joined-for/)\n",
